prompt:
You are contributing to TaskForge, a TypeScript + Bun CLI used in the RazorCascade memory reliability study.

Execution mode: cascade
Standardized task: 3. List, filter, and view tasks
Objective: Support querying tasks by status, priority, tags, and free-text search.

Context from prior work:
Goal: Provide a strongly-typed Task model and safe JSON-backed persistence for TaskForge using an app-local store (.taskforge/tasks.json).
Decisions: Use Bun for CLI/runtime compatibility and lightweight tooling; Persist all tasks in a single app-local JSON file at .taskforge/tasks.json; Version the on-disk schema (TaskStore) as version: 1; Define explicit Task types (id,title,status,priority,createdAt,updatedAt, optional description/completedAt); Validate loaded JSON strictly and reject malformed stores rather than silently repairing; Perform atomic writes via temp-file-in-same-dir + rename; Expose a command-agnostic storage API: listTasks, getTaskById, upsertTask, removeTask
Risks: Atomic rename semantics vary across filesystems/platforms and may break atomicity if temp file placed incorrectly; Strict validation can reject older or hand-edited stores unless a migration/versioning path is added; Concurrent writes/multi-process access are not addressed (current design assumes single-process CLI usage)
Snippets: const STORAGE_PATH = '.taskforge/tasks.json'; | type TaskStatus = 'todo' | 'in_progress' | 'done';
type TaskPriority = 'low' | 'medium' | 'high';
type Task = { id: string; title: string; status: TaskStatus; priority: TaskPriority; createdAt: string; updatedAt: string; description?: string; completedAt?: string; }; | type TaskStore = { version: 1; tasks: Task[] };
function createEmptyStore(): TaskStore { return { version: 1, tasks: [] }; } | async function saveStore(path: string, store: TaskStore) {
  const tmp = path + '.tmp';
  await Bun.write(tmp, JSON.stringify(store, null, 2));
  await Bun.rename(tmp, path);
}
Invariants: schema version = 1; storage file = .taskforge/tasks.json

Produce a concise engineering update that includes:
1. Goal
2. Proposed implementation details
3. Validation or testing
4. Risks
